@label "identifiable: getSymbol"
@description "containment-substrate Phase 2 Step 3 (design §10.3) — display math GLYPH for a type/former via the Symbolable typeclass. The general symbol projection: `getSymbol \"union\"` resolves the `Symbolable \"union\"` instance to `Just \"∪\"`. Pattern-matches on `dispatchLookupOne \"Symbolable\" formerName` and extracts the `symbol` field. Returns `Just String` on hit, `Nothing` on miss. The EXACT `getIcon` / `getEmoji` sibling (same dispatchLookupOne shape). Retires the formatter-hardcoded glyph strings (set-syntax.fenel formatter + ExpressionDisplay.tsx) into the representation substrate. Boundary adapter; dispatched via `dispatchedGetSymbol`."
@tags "engine" "identifiable" "representational" "dispatch" "containment-phase-2"
getSymbol : (formerName: String) -> Maybe String
getSymbol formerName = case dispatchLookupOne "Symbolable" formerName of
  Just methods -> Just methods.symbol
  Nothing -> Nothing

@label "identifiable: getEmoji"
@description "Phase 10b sub-step 1 — default emoji glyph for a type via the Emojiable typeclass. Sister to `getIcon`; used by chat / Telegram / terminal surfaces that prefer compact emoji. Returns `Just String` on hit, `Nothing` on miss. Boundary adapter; dispatched via `dispatchedGetEmoji`. Mirrors implementations/typescript/engine/src/identifiable.ts:getEmoji."
@tags "engine" "identifiable" "representational" "dispatch" "phase-10b"
